(572, 101, 'Event Schema for Event Detail Pages', '<p>Turn each event page into a complete, AI-ready source of truth.</p><p>When a visitor clicks into an event, your Event Detail page becomes the <strong>single most important page</strong> for that event. It&rsquo;s where real people decide whether to attend &ndash; and it&rsquo;s also where Search Engines and LLMs decide <strong>what this event actually is</strong>.</p><p>Brilliant Directories already provides a solid foundation with page-level structured data. This is intentionally general so it works for any niche and any type of directory. However, by default BD cannot know:</p><ul><li>How you position your events in your business model</li><li>Which fields matter most for your niche (pricing, seating, online links, sponsorships, etc.)</li><li>How you want AI systems and Search Engines to present each event</li></ul><p>So BD ships safe, broad schema. Our service takes the next step: we turn each Event Detail page into a <strong>complete, well-structured Event object</strong> that modern Search and AI tools can fully understand and trust.</p><p>The result?<br>That event is no longer just a nice landing page &ndash; it becomes a <strong>clean, machine-readable description of a real-world event</strong>, ready for rich search results, AI answers, and future integrations.</p><hr><h2>What This Implemented Schema Does (Detail Page)</h2><p>On the Event Detail page, we go beyond list-level data and describe the <strong>actual event itself</strong> as a single, authoritative Event object in JSON-LD.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;\">In practical terms, we:</p><ul><li>Define the page&rsquo;s main entity as a <strong>single Event</strong> (not just a generic page)</li><li>Map all key event fields, such as:<ul><li>Event Name</li><li>Description</li><li>Start Date &amp; End Date (with timezone)</li><li>Event Status (scheduled, postponed, cancelled)</li><li>Attendance Mode (offline, online, or mixed)</li><li>Venue Name</li><li>Full Postal Address</li><li>Images</li><li>Ticket / booking links</li><li>Organizer (Person or Organization)</li></ul></li><li>Keep everything in sync with your <strong>live BD event data</strong> &ndash; no manual re-entry</li><li>&nbsp;Respect your layout and design &ndash; markup is added behind the scenes</li></ul><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;\">Whenever your event includes more advanced details, we can also map additional fields like:</p><ul><li>Price tiers or different ticket types</li><li>Basic performer / host details</li><li>Online streaming URLs (for mixed or virtual events)</li><li>Event categories, tags, or audience type</li></ul><p>These enhancements are included whenever the data is available &ndash; the goal is to reflect the <strong>true richness</strong> of the event, not just the bare minimum.</p><hr><h2>Example JSON-LD for an Event Detail Page</h2><p>Below is a simplified example of the kind of schema we implement on an Event Detail page. In your live site, this would be injected as JSON-LD, generated directly from your BD event data:</p><table cellpadding=\"14\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(204, 204, 204); background: rgb(242, 242, 242); width: 100%;\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-family:Courier,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;\"><code>&nbsp;&lt;<span style=\"color:#c18401;background:transparent !important;\">script type</span>=&quot;application/ld+json&quot;&gt;&nbsp;<br> <span style=\"color:#50a14f;background:transparent !important;\">{&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@context&quot;: &quot;https://schema.org&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Event&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Snoopy on Ice&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;description&quot;: &quot;&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &quot;A family holiday ice show with Snoopy and friends, at Beverly Hills Ice Arena.&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;startDate&quot;: &quot;2025-12-20T19:00:00-08:00&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;endDate&quot;: &quot;2025-12-20T21:30:00-08:00&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;eventStatus&quot;: &quot;https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode&quot;,&nbsp;<br><code><br> <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">//appropriate fields from your BD events data fields as appropriate.</span></code> <br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;location&quot;: { &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Place&quot;, &nbsp;&nbsp;<br><code><br> <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">//appropriate fields from your BD events data fields as appropriate.</span></code> <br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;} &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;organizer&quot;: { &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Organization&quot;, &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;name&quot;: &quot;Holiday Events LA&quot;, &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://yourdirectory.com/organizers/holiday-events-la&quot; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;}, &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;offers&quot;: { &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Offer&quot; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://eventticketbooking.com/snoopy-on-ice&quot; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br><code><br> <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// and more elements from your BD datafields.</span></code> <br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;}, &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;audience&quot;: { &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;audienceType&quot;: &quot;Families and holiday visitors&quot; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;description&quot;: &quot;Ideal for families, holiday visitors, and local community groups&quot; &nbsp;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;},</span> <br> <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// + educating Google and LLMs about where to book or get tickets.</span></code><br><code><br> <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// and more.</span></code><br><code><br> <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// + additional fields we map to work 100% with all possible fields or</span>&nbsp;</code><br><code>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// datapoints your events have.</span> <br>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</code><br><code>&nbsp; &nbsp;<span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">&nbsp;// + we also advise you best strategies and apply our secret sauce on</span>&nbsp;</code><br><code>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// enhancing the power of schema relevant to your site (not just your industry)</span></code><br><code><br> &lt;/<span style=\"color:#c18401;background:transparent !important;\">script</span>&gt;&nbsp;</code></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:Courier,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;\"><br></td></tr></tbody></table><p><br></p><p>You can optionally pair this with enhanced schema on your Events Results page, so both the <strong>list view</strong> and the <strong>detail view</strong> tell the same clear story to Search Engines and LLMs.</p><p>Zero technical work for you.<br>Zero maintenance after setup.<br>Maximum SEO value.</p><hr><h2>How It Works (Simple &amp; Automatic)</h2><ol><li>We review your existing BD Event Detail page structure</li><li>We identify which fields are already available (dates, location, images, pricing, etc.)</li><li>We map those fields into a clean JSON-LD Event object following Schema.org guidelines</li><li>We integrate this schema so it updates automatically whenever you or your members edit an event.</li><li>We validate the output with Google&rsquo;s tools (and similar validators) to ensure everything is clean.</li><li>We leave your front-end design untouched &ndash; this is a behind-the-scenes upgrade.</li></ol><p>Zero extra data entry for you or your members.<br>Zero ongoing maintenance.<br>A single, trusted source of truth for each event.</p><hr><h2>How It Helps Your Members</h2><ul><li><strong>Clearer presence in search:</strong> Their individual events can be understood and highlighted as real-world events, not just generic pages.</li><li><strong>Better eligibility for rich results:</strong> Dates, venues, and ticket info can appear directly in Search and AI-powered experiences.</li><li><strong>Higher perceived professionalism:</strong> Events backed by correct schema feel more trustworthy to platforms and users alike.</li></ul><hr><h2>How It Helps You (Directory Owner)</h2><ul><li><strong>Stronger SEO &amp; AEO at the event level</strong> &ndash; each event becomes a fully described asset.</li><li><strong>More control over how events are understood&nbsp;</strong>by Search Engines and LLMs.</li><li><strong>Better support for monetization:</strong> Premium event listings gain a tangible value-add (&quot;your events get full schema done for you&quot;).</li><li><strong>Future-readiness:</strong> As AI search and assistants pull more directly from structured data, your events are already prepared.</li></ul><blockquote><strong>Note:</strong> Many clients start with Event Results Page schema and add Event Detail schema as the next step. Our <strong>SEO Consulting&nbsp;</strong>service can help determine the best approach for your site.</blockquote><hr><h2>🚀 Next Steps</h2><p><strong>Step 1: Click &ldquo;Order Now&rdquo; &amp; Submit a Few Details</strong><br>Share your name, email, website URL, and any basic info required to start your order.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Make the Payment to Confirm Your Order</strong><br>&nbsp;Once the payment is completed, your order is officially confirmed &mdash; no meeting or approval is needed to begin.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Expect Our Message for Final Inputs</strong><br>Within <strong>2 business days&nbsp;</strong>(usually &lt;24 hours), we&rsquo;ll reach out for anything we need &mdash; such as images, icons, branding elements, text, or your design/style preferences.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Quick Implementation After Your Approval</strong><br>We&rsquo;ll share the proposed plan, layout, or design options.&nbsp;<br>Once you confirm, <strong>we implement it at the earliest</strong> and handle everything end-to-end.</p><hr><h2>Ready to Make Each Event Page a Complete Entity?</h2><p>Click <strong>Order Now</strong> to add Event Detail Schema to your site &ndash; and turn every key event page into a fully structured, AI-ready source of truth.</p>', NULL, NULL, '20260613033220', '', 0, 'bc2b59e4824269283c320a7c9be9ba4d', 'solutions/event-schema-for-event-detail-pages', 1, 0, '', ' ', '', 4, 83, 'Enhance Conversions', '2026-06-13 07:35:44', '', '', '', ' ', '', '', '', '', 250.00, 0.00, 0.0, 0.0, NULL, 0, '', '0000-00-00', '', '', 0, NULL, 'fixed_price', 'quick_service', '', '', ' ', '12_weeks', ' ', ' ', ' ', 'Event Schema', 'Event Schema', 'semi_custom', ' ', 0.00, ' '),
(573, 101, 'Job Schema for Jobs Results Page', '<p>Turn every job listing into a complete, AI-understandable opportunity &mdash; directly from your results page.</p><p>Your Jobs Results page is not just a list of opportunities &mdash; it&rsquo;s a <strong>core informational asset</strong> that search engines and AI systems scan to understand:</p><ul><li>what jobs exist,</li><li>where they&rsquo;re located,</li><li>who&rsquo;s hiring,</li><li>what skills are needed, and</li><li>whether the job is relevant to a user&rsquo;s intent.</li></ul><p>Brilliant Directories already outputs <strong>basic list-level schema</strong> (such as <span style=\"font-size:15px !important;background:#ccc !important;padding:3px !important;\">CollectionPage</span> and<span style=\"font-size:15px !important;background:#ccc !important;padding:3px !important;\">&nbsp;ItemList</span>), which is excellent as a generic foundation. But BD cannot know your hiring model, niche, member data, or how job information is structured on your site.</p><p>That&rsquo;s where we step in.</p><p>This service enhances your Jobs Results page with<strong>&nbsp;clean, complete, search-ready JSON-LD Job</strong> Schema, fully aligned with your BD job data and compliant with modern SEO + AI standards.</p><p>The result?<br><br>Google and LLMs can correctly interpret each job listing on the page and treat them as real job opportunities, not just text blocks.</p><hr><h2>What This Implemented Schema Does</h2><p>Instead of Google guessing what each job listing means, we describe each job clearly with a structured <span style=\"font-size:15px !important;background:#ccc !important;padding:3px !important;\">JobPosting</span> object.</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;\">Our system automatically:</p><ul><li>Defines the page as a proper <strong>CollectionPage / ItemList</strong></li><li>Lists each visible job as a full <strong>JobPosting</strong> entity</li><li>Maps essential job fields:<ul><li>Job Title</li><li>Description (trimmed or structured)</li><li>Hiring Organization</li><li>Employment Type</li><li>Job Location (onsite, hybrid, or remote)</li><li>Posting Date</li><li>Valid Through (if available)</li><li>Main Job URL</li></ul></li><li>Pulls everything from your <strong>live BD job data</strong> &mdash; no manual input</li><li>Works with all themes, layouts, and custom designs</li></ul><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;\">When your directory uses richer job fields, we also map:</p><ul><li>Salary / compensation ranges</li><li>Benefits</li><li>Required skills</li><li>Experience level</li><li>Hiring region(s)</li><li>Job categories or tags</li></ul><p>We include these enhancements <strong>automatically</strong> whenever the data exists.</p><p>Your page looks exactly the same visually &mdash; the schema works behind the scenes.</p><blockquote><strong>Note:</strong> This setup covers all critical fields needed for Google&rsquo;s job indexing and AI understanding. For more advanced or industry-specific job schema enhancements, you can always reach out later.</blockquote><hr><h2>How It Works (Simple &amp; Automatic)</h2><ol><li>We detect all job listings currently shown on your results page.</li><li>We extract relevant data directly from BD&rsquo;s job fields.</li><li>We generate clean, validated JSON-LD JobPosting schema.</li><li>Google, LLMs, and AI systems immediately understand your jobs as structured objects.</li><li>Any new or updated job automatically appears in the schema.</li><li>No extra work for your members or team.</li></ol><hr><h2>Live Example (JSON-LD Preview)</h2><p>Below is a simplified example of the type of schema we implement for your <strong>Jobs Results Page.</strong> (In reality, additional mapped fields will appear based on your site&rsquo;s data.)</p><table cellpadding=\"14\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border: 1px solid rgb(204, 204, 204); background: rgb(242, 242, 242); width: 100%;\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"font-family:Courier,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;\"><code>&nbsp;&lt;<span style=\"color:#c18401;background:transparent !important;\">script type</span>=&quot;application/ld+json&quot;&gt;&nbsp;<br> <span style=\"color:#50a14f;background:transparent !important;\">{&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;{&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@context&quot;: &quot;https://schema.org&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@type&quot;: &quot;ItemList&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Latest Jobs&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; temListElemente : [&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;{&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@type&quot;: &quot;JobPosting&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;title&quot;: &quot;&quot;Full Stack PHP Developer&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;description&quot;: &quot;Work on high-performance web applications using PHP, JS, MySQL.&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;employmentType&quot;: &quot;FULL_TIME&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;hiringOrganization&quot;:{&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;@type&quot;&quot;: &quot;Organization&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;name&quot;: &quot;TechCorp Solutions&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://yourdirectory.com/companies/techcorp-solutions&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; },&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;jobLocation&quot;: {&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Place&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &quot;address&quot;:{&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;@type&quot;: &quot;PostalAddress&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;addressLocality&quot;: &quot;Bangalore&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;addressRegion&quot;: &quot;KA&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;addressCountry&quot;: &quot;IN&quot;,&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;}&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;},&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;datePosted&quot;: &quot;2025-01-10&quot;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;validThrough&quot;: &quot;2025-02-10&quot;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&quot;url&quot;: &quot;https://yourdirectory.com/jobs/full-stack-php-developer&quot;&nbsp;<br>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;}</span> <br> <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// + educating Google and LLMs about where to book or get tickets.</span></code><br><code><br> <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// and more.</span></code><br><code><br> <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// + additional fields we map to work 100% with all possible fields or</span>&nbsp;</code><br><code>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// datapoints your events have.</span> <br>&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</code><br><code>&nbsp; &nbsp;<span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">&nbsp;// + we also advise you best strategies and apply our secret sauce on</span>&nbsp;</code><br><code>&nbsp; &nbsp; <span style=\"color:#a0a1a7;background:transparent !important;\">// enhancing the power of schema relevant to your site (not just your industry)</span></code><br><code><br> &lt;/<span style=\"color:#c18401;background:transparent !important;\">script</span>&gt;&nbsp;</code></td></tr><tr><td style=\"font-family:Courier,monospace;font-size:14px;line-height:1.45;\"><br></td></tr></tbody></table><p><br>Zero manual work for you.<br>Zero ongoing maintenance.<br>Maximum SEO + AI impact.</p><hr><h2>How It Helps Your Members (Employers)</h2><ul><li><strong>Improved visibility</strong> for every job posted</li><li><strong>Higher credibility</strong> with structured employer + job data</li><li><strong>Better performance</strong> in AI-powered job search experiences</li><li><strong>More qualified applicants</strong> as search engines understand the job clearly</li></ul><hr><h2>How It Helps You (Directory Owner)</h2><ul><li>Stronger <strong>SEO &amp; AEO</strong> performance across your job listings</li><li>Full support for <strong>Google for Jobs</strong> eligibility (when applicable)</li><li>More valuable premium job posting packages</li><li>No technical steps or maintenance needed</li><li>Schema updates itself whenever jobs change</li></ul><blockquote><strong>Small note:</strong> Once your Jobs Results Schema is in place, most directories naturally proceed to add Job Detail Schema as the next upgrade. And if you ever want help prioritizing schema for multiple post types, our SEO Consulting service can guide you based on your goals.</blockquote><hr><h2>🚀 Next Steps</h2><p><strong>Step 1: Click &quot;Order Now&quot; &amp; Submit a Few Details</strong><br>Tell us your name, email, website URL, and any initial details.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Make the Payment to Confirm Your Order</strong><br>Once payment is complete, your job schema setup is queued immediately.</p><p><strong>Step 3: We Contact You for Final Inputs</strong><br>Within 24&ndash;48 hours, we reach out only if any clarification is needed.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Implementation Begins</strong><br>We validate, generate, and integrate all schemas. You approve, and it goes live.</p><hr><h2>Ready for Smarter Job Visibility?</h2><p>Click <strong>Order Now&nbsp;</strong>to activate structured Job Schema on your Jobs Results Page and unlock stronger visibility across Google + AI search.</p>', NULL, NULL, '20260613033220', '', 0, '52477079196e6705e309135358b44af9', 'solutions/job-schema-for-jobs-results-page', 1, 0, '', 'Order Now', '', 4, 83, 'Enhance Conversions', '2026-06-13 07:35:44', '', '', '', ' ', '', '', '', '', 250.00, 0.00, 0.0, 0.0, NULL, 0, '', '0000-00-00', '', '', 0, NULL, 'fixed_price', 'quick_service', '', '', ' ', '12_weeks', ' ', ' ', ' ', 'Job Schema', 'Job Schema', 'semi_custom', ' ', 0.00, ' '),
(574, 101, 'Essential SEO Audit', '<div class=\"essential-seo-audit\"><p><strong>Fast, expert SEO clarity for your Brilliant Directories website.</strong></p><p>The <strong>Essential SEO Audit</strong> is a one-time, focused review covering all SEO fundamentals that directly impact your directory&rsquo;s visibility, indexing, and daily discoverability. We go deep on the technical and on-page essentials &mdash; while keeping it practical for your execution budget.</p><p>This audit is perfect when you&#39;re launching, relaunching, or simply want clarity on what&rsquo;s working, what&rsquo;s not, and which fixes will move the needle fastest &mdash; all while staying inside a friendly execution budget.</p><hr><h2>What&#39;s Included in the Essential SEO Audit</h2><h3>1. Short Strategy Call (First Step)</h3><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;\">Before we review anything, we begin with a short strategy call to finalize:</p><ul><li>Your primary keyword/keyphrase</li><li>Supporting keyphrases</li><li>Keyphrases for the Homepage</li><li>Keyphrases for the Join Page</li><li>Member Results Page keyphrases</li><li>Member Profile (Detail Page) keyphrases</li><li>One core Post Type (Results + Detail) keyphrases</li></ul><p>This ensures the keywords you want to rank for are the exact ones your site is evaluated and reviewed for, making every recommendation relevant, sharp, and aligned to your goals.</p><hr><p style=\"font-size:25px;\">What We Review</p><h3>2. Tracking &amp; Indexing</h3><ul><li>GA4 / Google Tag Manager setup verification</li><li>Search Console setup &amp; verification</li><li>Sitemap submission &amp; indexing status</li><li>robots.txt crawl permissions</li><li>Suggestions on any important BD tools not configured<br><br></li></ul><h3>3. Meta Tags &amp; Page-Level SEO</h3><ul><li>Homepage</li><li>Up to 12 static pages</li><li>Member results page, including its categories, sub-categories, with and without locations</li><li>Member detail page (Member profiles)</li><li>One Core post type (Results + Detail)</li><li>Alignment to the keyphrases finalized during the strategy call<br><br></li></ul><h3>4. Content Structure &amp; Layout Review</h3><ul><li>H1/H2 hierarchy across all included pages</li><li>Structure &amp; SEO on 12 static pages</li><li>Member Results page structure</li><li>Member Profile (Detail) page structure</li><li>One Core Post Type structure (Results + Detail)</li><li>Keyword placement logic<br><br></li></ul><h3>5. URL Structure &amp; Internal Linking</h3><ul><li>Clean URLs verification</li><li>Category/city taxonomy patterns</li><li>Header/footer linking</li><li>Sidebar linking (if applicable)<br><br></li></ul><h3>6. Schema / Structured Data &mdash; Essential Coverage</h3><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;\">Schema checks on:</p><ul><li>Homepage</li><li>3&ndash;4 high-priority static pages</li><li>Member Results pages</li><li>Member Profile (Detail) pages</li></ul><p style=\"margin-bottom:0px;\">Schema types reviewed:</p><ul><li>Organization</li><li>LocalBusiness</li><li>Review/Ratings</li><li>Schema relevant to core post type used<br><br></li></ul><h3>7. Member Pages SEO Check</h3><ul><li>Member Results configuration</li><li>Member Profile configuration</li><li>Keyphrase alignment based on strategy call</li><li>Identification of obvious ranking blockers</li></ul><hr><h2>Essential vs Strategic SEO Audit (Comparison)</h2><p>After your Essential Audit is complete, you can either implement the fixes yourself or hire anyone you trust &mdash; most implementations fit comfortably within a <strong>$250&ndash;$500/mo</strong> budget. Our own monthly <a href=\"https://bdgrowthsuite.com/seo\" title=\"\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">SEO service</a> also starts in this friendly range, making ongoing improvements easy and affordable.</p><p>If your website is larger, your goals are bigger, and your implementation budget sits in the <strong>$1000&ndash;$2000/mo</strong> range, the <a href=\"https://bdgrowthsuite.com/tools/strategic-seo-audit-advanced\" title=\"\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Strategic SEO Audit (Advanced)&nbsp;</a>may be the better fit.</p><table class=\"table table-bordered seo-comparison\" style=\"margin-right: calc(0%); width: 100%;\"><thead><tr><th style=\"width: 25.0667%;border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\"><strong>Area</strong></th><th class=\"essential-col\" style=\"width: 37.6%; background-color: rgb(255, 247, 255);border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\"><strong>Essential Audit ($250)</strong><br><strong>(This very service)</strong><br></th><th style=\"width: 37.1931%;border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Strategic Audit (Advanced) ($1500)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style=\"width: 25.0667%;border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Delivery Time</td><td class=\"essential-col\" style=\"width: 37.6%; background-color: rgb(255, 247, 255);border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Under <strong>5 days</strong></td><td style=\"width: 37.1931%;border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Under <strong>2 weeks</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 25.0667%;border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Static Pages Reviewed</td><td class=\"essential-col\" style=\"width: 37.6%; background-color: rgb(255, 247, 255);border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Up to <strong>12</strong></td><td style=\"width: 37.1931%;border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Up to <strong>60</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 25.0667%;border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Post Types Reviewed</td><td class=\"essential-col\" style=\"width: 37.6%; background-color: rgb(255, 247, 255);border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\"><strong>1</strong></td><td style=\"width: 37.1931%;border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Up to <strong>4</strong></td></tr><tr><td style=\"width: 25.0667%;border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(224, 224, 224);\">Member Results Pages</td><td class=\"essential-col\" style=\"width: 37.